{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":97969,"duration_api_ms":150070,"num_turns":7,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c178fd86-7b9e-4a0b-ad92-96bb4abb345c","total_cost_usd":0.4586833,"usage":{"input_tokens":876,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30404,"cache_read_input_tokens":82076,"output_tokens":4023,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30404,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":114,"outputTokens":9204,"cacheReadInputTokens":348663,"cacheCreationInputTokens":33332,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.12266529999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":876,"outputTokens":4023,"cacheReadInputTokens":82076,"cacheCreationInputTokens":30404,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.336018,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All five amendments are validated by code inspection. Two are low-risk comment/documentation fixes for non-obvious ordering dependencies (fr-1-6104f9a9, fr-1-4b75eb30). Three identify real modeling bugs: stale substrate area constants (fr-1-cc4cd8d6), stale crowding index after trim actions (fr-1-a0ecdac3), and incorrect light attenuation depth for SubstrateSurface (fr-1-c473b4ce). I agree with the planner's accept positions on all five.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-6104f9a9","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: `update_daily_filter_clogging` mutates `filter_state.clogging_index` (nitrogen_cycle.rs:630-631), and `compute_filter_media` reads it (habitat.rs:164) to derive FilterMedia oxygen exposure. The dual-refresh pattern (engine.rs:369-382) is correct but non-obvious — without a comment, a future contributor could reasonably delete the second refresh as redundant. Minimal cost, high value for preventing a subtle regression."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-4b75eb30","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: the habitat registry reads geometry, hardware, filter_state, plant_guilds, and substrate_layers — but NOT detritus totals or animal counts. Feed, SiphonDetritus, AddShrimp, and RemoveShrimp only modify detritus and animal state, so the unconditional refresh at engine.rs:727 is indeed a no-op for those actions. A comment explaining the simplicity-over-precision tradeoff is the right minimal fix; making the refresh conditional is also valid but riskier if new actions are added later."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-cc4cd8d6","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: SubstrateSurface returns full footprint when any layer exists (habitat.rs:205-209), ignoring actual substrate depth or coverage. SubstrateDeep sums stored `colonizable_area_cm2` values that are baked in at materialization time (lib.rs:748-754) and never updated. The default layer hardcodes 100.0 cm² (substrate.rs:24-33) with no relationship to actual tank geometry. A zero-depth layer would still report full surface area. These are real modeling defects that survive `refresh_habitat_registry()` because the refresh reads stale stored constants."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-a0ecdac3","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: compute_habitat_registry averages plant_guilds[].crowding_index (habitat.rs:85-94) to derive avg_crowding, which attenuates light for GlassHardscape, PlantSurfaces, and SubstrateSurface habitats. But crowding_index is only recomputed in step_daily_plants (plant_growth.rs:24-30), while trim actions (engine.rs:608-649) reduce biomass and immediately trigger refresh_habitat_registry (engine.rs:727) with stale crowding values. The placeholder 0.1 at materialization (lib.rs:787) also means the initial registry is computed with wrong crowding. Recomputing crowding on the refresh path would fix both cases."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-c473b4ce","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: depth_attenuation is `(1.0 - mean_depth_cm() / 60.0).clamp(0.1, 1.0)` (habitat.rs:117), and mean_depth_cm() just returns fill_height_cm (geometry.rs:60-61). SubstrateSurface represents the top of the substrate bed, which sits at fill_height - substrate_depth from the water surface. Using full fill height ignores that the substrate displaces water, making light reach the substrate surface through a shorter water column. substrate_depth_cm() already exists (state.rs:172-177) and can derive the correct effective water depth. This is a clear physics/modeling bug."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"6d99b9ba-cd2a-4484-a5f1-f9de373ad994"}
